# Components passed as values. def tunic is a red 20x20 rect, def cape is a gold 30x14 rect, and def doll draws a circle head of radius 14 in its tone (default blue) with a parameter `outfit` that defaults to none (draws nothing)
# and, when set to a component, is placed with `outfit` below the head. doll also has `fx outline 3` in its body, so every instance gets a ring 3 wide around everything it draws.
# Undocumented, current behavior: on a def instance with no fill of its own, the default outline color is line() of the first fill in the instance's subtree. That is navy for the blue-headed dolls 1-3 and dark green for doll 4, including around its red tunic.
# 256x192 artboard, two rows of four 64-wide cells; the top row is 96 tall, dolls centered in it.
# Left to right: doll with the default outfit none (only a blue circle head with a dark ring, nothing below it); doll outfit:tunic (the same head with a red square below it, the ring following the head and square together);
# doll outfit:cape (the same head with a wider-than-tall gold rect below it, ringed); doll tone:p.green outfit:tunic (green head, the same red square, with a dark green ring).
# Bottom row, left to right: doll outfit:tunic with a call-site `fx shadow 8,8 blur:0 color:p.ink` after the def's outline (a hard ink copy of the whole outlined silhouette, ring included, offset 8 right and 8 down behind the doll; the effect order is def outline first, call-site shadow second).
@artboard 256x192
@target components/values_fx.png

def tunic size:20
  rect 100%,100% fill:p.red

def cape size:30x14
  rect 100%,100% fill:p.gold

def doll size:56 tone:p.blue outfit:none
  circle 14 at:0,-14 fill:tone
  outfit at:0,12
  fx outline 3

doll at:32,48 name:d1
doll at:96,48 outfit:tunic name:d2
doll at:160,48 outfit:cape name:d3
doll at:224,48 tone:p.green outfit:tunic name:d4
doll at:32,144 outfit:tunic name:d5
  fx shadow 8,8 blur:0 color:p.ink
